From af8a9d0568f4552596b9d5f4b6e84af85d171070 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pannal <1359593+pannal@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 02:11:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [ClearKey] Backport CBCS support for HLS+ClearKey playback

Ports upstream master commit 37e01a06 ([ClearKey] Implemented CBCS support)
onto the Omega branch so HLS streams using SAMPLE-AES (cbcs) with ClearKey
can be decrypted. Omega-side HLSTree already mapped SAMPLE-AES to AES_CBC
but the ClearKey decrypter:
  1) was hardcoded to refuse anything but AES_CTR, and
  2) created a single CTR-only AP4 decrypter at construction time and
     ignored the per-fragment CryptoInfo handed to SetFragmentInfo.

Rewrites CClearKeyCencSingleSampleDecrypter to a pool-based, lazy-create
flow (CTR or CBC chosen from cryptoInfo.m_mode, with resetIvEachSubsample
for CBCS). License-request flow is kept unchanged (rapidjson, same constructor
signatures, same Kodi-property semantics); storage moves to a raw-bytes
KID/KEY map. The decrypter falls back to the single available key when
EXT-X-KEY carries no KEYID (typical HLS+CK identity-keyformat case).

p3i-only; will not be sent upstream (Omega is in maintenance, the fix is
already on master 22.x).
